        "source_sha256": "a3256af1aeb97da435c3255743a67588b4adbd01ee6f027dd20dd0dd3f0a4118",
        "text": "- Meet Zac\n- Issues\n- News\n- Volunteer\n- Donate\n# Solutions and leadership for all\nWhen our family moved to Pleasant Hill in 2003, we quickly discovered what makes this community so special. It is a safe, welcoming place with a strong sense of community—and more than two decades later, I remain committed to preserving those qualities while preparing our city for the future.\nI am seeking re-election to the Pleasant Hill City Council now in District 3 because I believe experienced, pragmatic leadership matters—especially as our city faces important decisions about its financial future, housing, economic vitality and the services our residents depend on.\nAs your Mayor and City Councilmember, I have worked hard to find practical solutions to today's challenges while keeping an eye on tomorrow. I'm proud of the progress we've made, including adopting our 2040 General Plan and Housing Element, Bicycle & Pedestrian Master Plan--and most recently--our Climate Action Plan, investing in our infrastructure and public safety, supporting local businesses, and planning for a more sustainable and inclusive community.\nThere is more work ahead. I remain committed to:\n- Protecting Pleasant Hill's fiscal future by responsibly managing taxpayer dollars, controlling costs and strengthening our local economy.\n- Keeping our community safe, welcoming and inclusive for residents, families and businesses.\n- Supporting local businesses and creating opportunities for them to thrive.\n- Planning thoughtfully for housing and growth while preserving the qualities that make Pleasant Hill such a desirable place to live.\n- Delivering effective city services and making smart investments in the infrastructure our community relies upon.\nPleasant Hill is a special place. I would be honored to earn your vote for District 3 and continue working with you to keep it that way while building a strong and sustainable future for our city.\nNot sure which district you reside in? Visit www.phillca.gov/mydistrict to find out.\nMake a Donation\nOur campaign is powered by your donations.\n$10 $25 $50 $100 $250 $500 Other\nSign Up for Updates\nFirst name Last name Email Zip/Postal Message\nThanks for signing up!\n- Voter Information\n- Endorsements\n- Events\n- Photos\n- Contact\nPaid for by Zac Shess for Pleasant Hill City Council 2026, FPPC ID 1448635\nPowered by CampaignPartner.com\n- Home\n- Meet Zac\n- Issues\n- Endorsements\n- Donate\n- Volunteer\n- Events\n- Contact\nClose Menu",
        "text_limited": false,
        "title": "Zac Shess for Pleasant Hill City Council",
